# CODEOWNERS
#
# Purpose: Require explicit review by the repository owner for any change
# that could introduce supply‑chain risk, alter build/deploy behavior, leak
# secrets, or silently modify game logic/content in privileged ways.
#
# Notes:
# - GitHub uses the last matching pattern for ownership resolution. Since all
#   patterns map to the same owner right now, order is mainly documentary.
# - Keep the list tight to reduce review noise. Do NOT add a catch‑all * rule
#   unless you truly want to review every change.
# - To add additional reviewers, append them to the line (e.g. @amoffat @team/sec @user2).

# --- CI / Automation Workflow Definitions ---
.github/**              @amoffat

# --- Dev Container & Development Environment ---
.devcontainer/**                 @amoffat

# --- Build / Tooling Config (root + internal) ---
postcss.config.cjs              @amoffat
engine_version.txt              @amoffat
upgrade.patch                   @amoffat

# Internal build system / project tooling
.internal/package.json          @amoffat
.internal/package-lock.json     @amoffat
.internal/eslint.config.js      @amoffat
.internal/vite.config.ts        @amoffat
.internal/tsconfig*.json        @amoffat

# Scripts capable of mutating artifacts or publishing
.internal/scripts/**            @amoffat

# Catch specific high‑risk file types at root (add more as needed)
/*.py                           @amoffat
/*.sh                           @amoffat

# Optional: uncomment to guard repository documentation changes
# README.md                      @amoffat

# End of CODEOWNERS